  "markdown": "Contact\n\n# Start your project.\n\nA short note is enough: the building, the material if you know it, and the date you have in mind. Tell us whether to reply by email or by phone, not both. Photographs, drawings and PDFs help, and are optional.\n\nAbout the page you chose\n\nInclude this topic with your note, or remove it. You can change the service below.\n\nRemove this topic\n\nWhich service? Optional\n\n- Not sure yet\n- Wallcovering installation or sourcing\n- Architectural and furniture film wrapping\n- Window film\n- Exterior decorating\n- Care or repair of existing work\n\nYour material choices\n\nRemove these choices\n\nAdd a fuller brief\n\nThe short note below is enough. The fuller brief is optional, and you can leave any answer as “not sure”.\n\nStep 1 of 4\n\nYour project\n\nWho is enquiring?\n\n- Not sure\n- Homeowner\n- Designer or architect\n- Property developer or main contractor\n- Hotel or property operator\n- Other commercial project\n\nWhat do you need?\n\n- Not sure\n- I already have the material\n- Help me choose, then install it\n- Advice\n- Removal or preparation\n- Repair\n\nArea or postcode district\n\nRooms\n\n- Not sure\n- One room\n- Several rooms\n- A whole home\n- A hotel floor or more\n\nWho is supplying the material?\n\nProgramme or tender date\n\nSpecification, drawing revisions or open questions\n\nWalls and materials\n\nProduct, brand or code, if you know it\n\nWalls, heights or condition\n\nTiming\n\nWhen would you like to start?\n\nAccess, occupied rooms, or site limits\n\nBudget\n\n- Prefer to discuss\n- Prefer to discuss\n- I have a range and will say so in the note\n\nCheck the note below, then send. You can go back and change an answer. Nothing is stored in the page address.\n\nBack\n\nContinue\n\nHow we should reply\n\nName\n\nReply by\n\nEmail\n\nPhone\n\nEmail\n\nPhone\n\nNote\n\nPhotographs or a PDF, if you have them\n\nPhone photographs and drawings help. JPEG, PNG, WebP, HEIC, HEIF and PDF. Up to 8 files and 10 MB in total. You do not have to attach anything to write to us. If a file will not send, email info@mrwallcover.com.\n\nHow did you hear about us? Optional\n\n- Prefer not to say / not sure\n- Google Search\n- Instagram\n- A recommendation\n- We have worked together before\n- A designer, architect or contractor\n- Somewhere else\n\nEmail me occasional Mr Wallcover project and material updates. Optional; withdraw at any time.\n\nSeparate from your enquiry. You can withdraw by [emailing us](mailto:info@mrwallcover.com).\n\nYour note is sent to info@mrwallcover.com with a reference. Dorin Burcus reads it. If you have not heard back, email that address directly.\n\nWe use the details you send to respond to this request. [Read the privacy notice](https://www.mrwallcover.com/privacy/).\n\nStart your project\n\nThis form needs JavaScript. Email info@mrwallcover.com instead.\n\nOr go direct. The phone is answered by Dorin Burcus himself; the number is shown on request.\n\n[info@mrwallcover.com](mailto:info@mrwallcover.com)\n\n[WhatsApp us](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/) [Book a call](https://calendar.google.com/calendar/appointments/schedules/AcZssZ3Aimn0z8hHnmqvg0zrZGV0Zt2PVu8UNOZPnrUJ34DgohlLAwO6xXIPaeH3mr_rE_JeJHr_DzUk)\n\nCalls Mon–Fri, 9am–5pm UK.\n\n[Instagram @mrwallcover](https://www.instagram.com/mrwallcover/)\n\n## What to send for a fast quote\n\nNone of this is required: a short note is enough to start. Each item you can send now is a question we will not need to ask later.\n\n**The building and the rooms.** The address or area, the rooms, and a rough idea of the walls involved.\n\n**The product code and colourway.** Or a link to the paper. A code is more useful than a description, because the code decides the labour. [Why the code matters](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/installation-cost/).\n\n**Whether you already have it.** If the paper is already bought, a photograph of the roll labels helps; if it is still to be ordered, say so and we can source it.\n\n**Photographs of the walls as they are.** Phone photographs are fine. They show the preparation the walls will need, which can be the larger part of the time on a period wall. [Wall preparation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/wall-preparation/).\n\n**Drawings or wall sizes, if you have them.** Elevations, or widths and heights. We measure on site, or from drawings when the programme needs it.\n\n**Access and occupancy.** Stairs, high walls, working hours, and whether the house or hotel stays in use while we work.\n\n**The date you have in mind.** We will say whether it is realistic. On a tender, give both the tender deadline and the start date.\n\n## A useful first brief\n\nIllustrative project brief\n\nPause motion\n\nTell us the area, the rooms or rough scope, the paper or material you have in mind, and your preferred timing. Photographs or drawings can follow by email.\n\nYou do not need every answer yet. We can establish the details together.\n\nWhat do you need?\n\n## Five ways to begin.\n\n### I already have the wallpaper\n\nInstallation, with the product you have bought. Measurements can wait.\n\n### Help me choose and install it\n\nA material family, a sample in the room, then the hang.\n\n### I am specifying a project\n\nSend the room schedule, drawings and the specification. Unknowns can stay blank.\n\n### A hotel or contractor package\n\nAccess, programme and who supplies the material.\n\n### Aftercare or a repair\n\nA separate note for existing work. A photograph tells us whether it is the hang or the building.\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last reviewed 9 October 2026\n",
